    {
      "kind": "grammar_point",
      "external_id": "g_c1_weighing_evidence_advanced_reporting",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-weighing-evidence-01",
        "slug": "c1-weighing-evidence-advanced-reporting",
        "title": "Advanced reporting verbs",
        "rule_summary": "Choose reporting verbs such as acknowledge, maintain, concede, dispute, imply, and caution to represent a source's stance accurately.",
        "explanation": {
          "fa": "برای بازتاب دقیق موضع منبع از فعل‌هایی مثل acknowledge، maintain، concede، dispute، imply و caution استفاده می‌کنیم."
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "en": "The author acknowledges the limitation but maintains that the trend is meaningful.",
            "fa": "نویسنده محدودیت را می‌پذیرد اما همچنان معتقد است روند معنادار است."
          },
          {
            "en": "The report cautions against treating correlation as proof of cause.",
            "fa": "گزارش هشدار می‌دهد همبستگی را به‌عنوان اثبات علت در نظر نگیریم."
          }
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "grammar_point",
      "external_id": "g_c1_weighing_evidence_advanced_hedging",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-weighing-evidence-02",
        "slug": "c1-weighing-evidence-advanced-hedging",
        "title": "Advanced hedging and calibration",
        "rule_summary": "Calibrate certainty with expressions such as arguably, broadly speaking, tends to, appears to, and cannot entirely be ruled out.",
        "explanation": {
          "fa": "در C1 میزان قطعیت را با عبارت‌هایی مثل arguably، broadly speaking، tends to، appears to و cannot entirely be ruled out دقیق تنظیم می‌کنیم."
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "en": "The change appears to have improved access, although the evidence is still limited.",
            "fa": "به نظر می‌رسد این تغییر دسترسی را بهتر کرده، هرچند شواهد هنوز محدود است."
          },
          {
            "en": "That explanation cannot entirely be ruled out.",
            "fa": "نمی‌توان آن توضیح را کاملاً منتفی دانست."
          }
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "grammar_point",
      "external_id": "g_c1_weighing_evidence_concession_rebuttal",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-weighing-evidence-03",
        "slug": "c1-weighing-evidence-concession-rebuttal",
        "title": "Concession followed by rebuttal",
        "rule_summary": "Acknowledge a reasonable opposing point before limiting it or presenting a stronger counterargument.",
        "explanation": {
          "fa": "ابتدا یک نکته منطقی از طرف مقابل را می‌پذیریم و سپس دامنه آن را محدود می‌کنیم یا پاسخ قوی‌تری می‌دهیم."
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "en": "Granted, the process is faster; that does not necessarily make it fairer.",
            "fa": "درست است که روند سریع‌تر است؛ اما لزوماً عادلانه‌تر نیست."
          },
          {
            "en": "While that concern is valid, it overlooks the cost of doing nothing.",
            "fa": "با اینکه آن نگرانی معتبر است، هزینه هیچ کاری نکردن را نادیده می‌گیرد."
          }
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "external_id": "d_c1_weighing_evidence_scene_1",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-weighing-evidence-01",
        "title": "Weighing Evidence: part 1",
        "setting": "seminar break",
        "cefr": "C1",
        "topic": "simple-messages",
        "characters": [
          "Ella",
          "Amir"
        ],
        "turns": [
          {
            "order": 1,
            "speaker": "Ella",
            "text": "Which assumption is doing most of the work here?",
            "translation_fa": "کدوم فرض بیشترین نقش رو در این استدلال داره؟"
          },
          {
            "order": 2,
            "speaker": "Amir",
            "text": "The evidence is reasonably robust on the overall trend, but much weaker on the explanation for it.",
